phrase_word_fields.plain, line 2: Write "the total of" instead of "the totals of", or use 's for a field called "totals".

    show the totals of sales
         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Try one of these:
    show the total of sales
  or
    show sales' totals
Why: "the totals of" looks like Plain's own phrase "the total of", so it could mean that phrase or a field called "totals". Plain never guesses which one you mean.

phrase_word_fields.plain, line 3: Use 's for a field called "items".

    show the items of sales
         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Try this:
    show sales' items
Why: "items" is a word of Plain's own phrases, like "the first 2 items of". With 's it can only mean a field.

phrase_word_fields.plain, line 4: Write "the characters of" instead of "the letters of".

    show the letters of "abc"
         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Try this:
    show the characters of "abc"
Why: Plain says "the characters of" for the letters, digits and spaces of a text.

phrase_word_fields.plain, line 5: Write "the largest of" instead of "the max of", or use 's for a field called "max".

    show the max of the amounts of sales
         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Try one of these:
    show the largest of the amounts of sales
  or
    show (the amounts of sales)'s max
Why: Plain says "the largest of" for the largest number in a list.

phrase_word_fields.plain, line 6: Write "a random item from" instead of "a random item of".

    show a random item of sales
         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Try this:
    show a random item from sales
Why: Plain picks an item by chance from a list, as in: a random item from colors

